# Wave W17-G (Route 33): drip tree — a dark rain tree with a heavy wet canopy, droplets still falling from its rim, on rain turf (ground baked in). First drawing read as bare trunks on the dark wet turf (canopy highlight sat at the turf’s own value) — redrawn once before landing at full canopy mass with the highlight lifted, the cliffpine discipline.
